<% content_for :title, "Open Scriptorium" %>

<%# ============================================================
  # Hero
  # ============================================================ %>
<section class="border-b border-[var(--color-rule)]">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 py-20 sm:py-28 grid sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-10 gap-y-6 items-center">

    <%# Decorative illuminated initial — the same S as the navbar/favicon %>
    <div class="hidden sm:block">
      <%= inline_svg "dropcap-S", class: "dropcap-hero" %>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-[var(--color-ink)] text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-tight">
        An open reading room <br class="hidden sm:inline">
        for scripture and the voices that have read it.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] font-serif leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Parallel translations of the Hebrew Bible, the Greek New Testament,
        the Septuagint, and various apocryphal texts &mdash; alongside
        historical commentary from Philo, Josephus, Origen, and later
        patristic and post-patristic voices &mdash; all
        <%= link_to "freely licensed", principles_path,
              class: "underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[var(--color-link)]" %>,
        all cross&#8209;referenced down to the verse.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
        <%= link_to "Start reading →", works_path,
              class: "inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-page)] font-serif text-lg rounded hover:opacity-90" %>
        <%= link_to "how it works", about_architecture_path,
              class: "text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] font-serif italic underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[var(--color-link)]" %>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<%# ============================================================
  # Epigraph — the two opening lines as a quiet centered block
  # ============================================================ %>
<section class="border-b border-[var(--color-rule)]">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 py-16 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] mb-6">
      The beginning
    </p>

    <p class="font-hebrew text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)] leading-loose" lang="he">
      בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] italic font-serif">
      Genesis 1:1 (Westminster Leningrad Codex)
    </p>

    <hr class="my-8 border-[var(--color-rule)] w-16 mx-auto">

    <p class="font-greek text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)] leading-loose">
      Ἐν ἀρχῇ ἦν ὁ λόγος.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] italic font-serif">
      John 1:1 (Nestle 1904)
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ============================================================
  # Three-column "what's here" overview
  # ============================================================ %>
<section>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 py-16">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-8">In the corpus</h2>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-x-8 gap-y-10 font-serif">
      <article>
        <h3 class="text-lg text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-2">Scripture in three languages</h3>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed text-sm">
          The Berean Standard Bible in English; the Westminster Leningrad
          Codex for the Hebrew Bible; Nestle&rsquo;s 1904 and the
          Robinson&ndash;Pierpont Byzantine Textform for the Greek New
          Testament; Rahlfs&rsquo; Septuagint and Brenton&rsquo;s English
          translation of it for the deuterocanon and the Old Greek
          tradition. Every verse aligns to the same canonical reference
          so they can be read
          <%= link_to "in parallel", parallel_chapter_path("genesis", 1, works: "bsb,wlc"),
                class: "underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[var(--color-link)]" %>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] italic">
          Six scripture works loaded. Cross-scheme verse alignment
          (LXX&nbsp;↔&nbsp;MT&nbsp;↔&nbsp;KJV) live via TVTMS.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3 class="text-lg text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-2">Commentary in the same schema</h3>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed text-sm">
          Historical commentary &mdash; Philo, Josephus, Origen, the
          Ante-Nicene Fathers, and later voices &mdash; lives in the
          same tables as scripture, with cross&#8209;references that
          work in both directions. A note on Genesis 1:1 from Origen
          and a note on Genesis 1:1 from a graduate student in 2026
          are the same kind of object: anchored to a canonical
          reference, found by one indexed lookup, freely citable.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3 class="text-lg text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-2">Scripture must be free</h3>

        <figure class="mb-3 pl-3 border-l-2 border-[var(--color-rule)]">
          <blockquote class="text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] text-sm leading-snug">
            <p>&hellip;Write the vision, and make it plain upon tables,
            that a man may read it swiftly.</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="text-xs italic mt-0.5 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
            &mdash; Habakkuk 2:2 (JPS 1917)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="mb-3 pl-3 border-l-2 border-[var(--color-rule)]">
          <blockquote class="text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] text-sm leading-snug">
            <p>&hellip;freely ye have received, freely give.</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="text-xs italic mt-0.5 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
            &mdash; Matthew 10:8 (KJV)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed text-sm">
          Every text in the corpus is under a license that meets the
          <a href="https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/free-sw.en.html" class="underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[var(--color-link)]">FSF definition of free software</a>
          or the SIL Open Font License. Source code is available
          <a href="https://git.sr.ht/~sethkush/openscriptorium" class="underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[var(--color-link)]">on sr.ht</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
